       \"rxn_004\",\n        \"rxn_005\",\n        \"rxn_011\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Specify catalyst and operating conditions establishing selective rxn_005 rather than assuming hydrothermal hydrogenation preserves the aldehyde.\",\n        \"Describe imine formation and cyanide capture as coupled equilibria, with ammonia activity, cyanide speciation and water activity constrained.\",\n        \"Demonstrate the transition from Strecker-compatible conditions to a hydrolysis regime that releases valine without excessive decomposition.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.76,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.48,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.82,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_012\": 0.75,\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.64\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.65,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.8,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.43,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.62,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.61,\n      \"feedback\": \"The imine-capture sequence and hydantoin connectivity are chemically appropriate. Nevertheless, rxn_005 lacks an established selective catalyst/environment combination, while rxn_012 and rxn_013 lack conditions demonstrating productive hydantoin formation and complete release of valine. This is an alternative sequence within the same Strecker-based branch, not independent experimental confirmation of the network.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_004\",\n        \"rxn_005\",\n        \"rxn_012\",\n        \"rxn_013\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Validate the aldol and selective hydrogenation sequence with realistic catalysts and competing-product measurements.\",\n        \"Quantify transient imine capture and subsequent carbonation under explicitly compatible conditions.\",\n        \"Track hydantoin ring opening, N-carbamoyl intermediate conversion and valine survival during h