y physically justified aldehyde transfer and separate hydrolysis conditions, including product recovery measurements.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P10\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.38,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.82,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_012\": 0.75,\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.64\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.57,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.76,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.37,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.55,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.55,\n      \"feedback\": \"The pathway identifies appropriate aminonitrile and hydantoin intermediates, but target production remains conditional on selective alcohol dehydrogenation and complete hydantoin hydrolysis. The explicit imine entry is mechanistically reasonable but does not constitute independent evidence relative to P8. Compatible conditions and intermediate survival across the proposed settings have not been demonstrated.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_006\",\n        \"rxn_012\",\n        \"rxn_013\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Establish the catalyst, energy input and hydrogen-removal mechanism supporting rxn_006.\",\n        \"Demonstrate aminonitrile formation followed by hydantoin formation under specified, compatible solution conditions.\",\n        \"Quantify hydantoin hydrolysis kinetics, intermediate accumulation and valine stability under the proposed hydrothermal conditions.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"best_pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n  \"overall_confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"network_feedback\": \"The network is structurally strong: all 20 molecule nodes and 13 reaction nodes are connected, molecule IDs are consistent, and the ten listed sequences lead formally to the correctly identified racemic valine target. Accepting the deterministic balance check, there are no mass or charge violations. The reported coefficients should be made explicit for rxn_0