ariant of the sulfur-reservoir route; selective sulfur replacement is particularly uncertain.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_009", "rxn_011", "rxn_008"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_007", "mol_009", "mol_011", "mol_010"]}, {"pathway_id": "P8", "name": "Cyanohydrin entry through a sulfide reservoir and alkaline hydrolysis", "description": "Cyanohydrin-mediated Strecker entry is followed by the same speculative alkaline aminothioamide processing as P7. The sequence is graph-distinct but supplies no independent evidence for those shared reactions.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_009", "rxn_011", "rxn_008"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_009", "mol_011", "mol_010"]}, {"pathway_id": "P9", "name": "Imine-entry hydantoin route with explicit deprotection", "description": "Imine-derived aminonitrile incorporates a temporary CO2-derived carbamoyl carbon to form hydantoin. Separate ring opening and decarbamoylation restore the C5 valine skeleton. This is a conditional laboratory-grounded branch, not a demonstrated prebiotic sequence; both deprotection stages require validation.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_012", "rxn_013", "rxn_014"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_007", "mol_009", "mol_012", "mol_013"]}, {"pathway_id": "P10", "name": "Cyanohydrin-entry hydantoin route with explicit deprotection", "description": "Cyanohydrin-mediated Strecker equilibration precedes hydantoin capture, alkaline ring opening and acidic decarbamoylation. The lost carbon is specifically the added carbamoyl carbon, unlike the review's unsupported C6 aminonitrile shortening. The same unresolved hydrolysis and environmental-integration limitations as P9 apply.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_012", "rxn_013", "rxn_014"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_009", "mol_012", "mol_013"]}], "hub_molecules": ["mol_009", "mol_010", "mol_011"], "convergence_points": [{"molecule_id": "mol_009", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_002"